 "line.town.bookclub.faust.1": "January is Faust's month. Who got through the Prologue in Heaven?",
 "line.town.bookclub.faust.2": "I read it as a girl. The old scholar in his study, that's me now.",
 "line.town.bookclub.faust.3": "He knows everything and is still bored. I get that far too well.",
 "line.town.bookclub.faust.4": "A poodle that isn't a poodle. The best bug in literature.",
 "line.town.bookclub.faust.5": "\"Stay, moment\" — and we haven't even reached the bargain yet.",
 "reading.club.hero.faust.1": "I liked Mephistopheles best. At least he's honest about being bored.",
 "reading.club.hero.faust.2": "And now I say \"Stay, moment\" by the sea at sunset.",
 "line.town.bookclub.queen_of_spades.1": "February, Pushkin, The Queen of Spades. Short, but what a blizzard.",
 "line.town.bookclub.queen_of_spades.2": "Hermann worked out everything except people. Like many of my pupils.",
 "line.town.bookclub.queen_of_spades.3": "Three cards and not one to spare for a mistake. Harsh.",
 "line.town.bookclub.queen_of_spades.4": "He wants an algorithm for winning. I understand him, honestly.",
 "line.town.bookclub.queen_of_spades.5": "Pushkin writes so fast it's frightening. Not one word too many.",
 "reading.club.hero.queen_of_spades.1": "I finished it at night and couldn't sleep for ages.",
 "reading.club.hero.queen_of_spades.2": "I think the countess winked at more than just Hermann.",
 "line.town.bookclub.ibsen_doll.1": "March: A Doll's House. It's a play, read it aloud, it's better.",
 "line.town.bookclub.ibsen_doll.2": "Nora and the macaroons she's not allowed. A trifle, and so much said.",
 "line.town.bookclub.ibsen_doll.3": "Her husband calls her his squirrel. I'm uneasy already, in act one.",
 "line.town.bookclub.ibsen_doll.4": "The play is a hundred and forty years old and reads like a chat log.",
 "line.town.bookclub.ibsen_doll.5": "Ibsen puts in one chair and one secret, and the room is full.",
 "reading.club.hero.ibsen_doll.1": "I read it on a bench and nearly shouted across the park.",
 "reading.club.hero.ibsen_doll.2": "The door slamming at the end is the best sound I've ever read.",
 "line.town.bookclub.time_machine.1": "April: Wells, The Time Machine. There'll be an argument, I can tell.",
 "line.town.bookclub.time_machine.2": "He tells it to his guests over supper. That's how I tell my grandchildren.",
 "line.town.bookclub.time_machine.3": "The fourth dimension on page one, and nobody leaves the table.",
 "line.town.bookclub.time_machine.4": "An ivory lever and quartz. I want the blueprints and there are none.",
 "line.town.bookclub.time_machine.5": "The boldest thing in Wells: his guests don't believe him. Very human.",
 "reading.club.hero.time_machine.1": "Now I look at the clock on the square and think where I'd go.",
 "reading.club.hero.time_machine.2": "I was scared for Weena. Really scared.",
 "line.town.bookclub.two_cities.1": "May: Dickens. \"It was the best of times...\" Remember?",
 "line.town.bookclub.two_cities.2": "A first sentence a page long. We never set dictations like that.",
 "line.town.bookclub.two_cities.3": "A mail coach in the fog and everyone afraid of everyone. Atmosphere.",
 "line.town.bookclub.two_cities.4": "\"Recalled to life\" — Dickens has better passwords than I do.",
 "line.town.bookclub.two_cities.5": "Dickens was paid by the word. Sometimes you can tell. The fog is worth it.",
 "reading.club.hero.two_cities.1": "Madame Defarge and her knitting are scarier than any villain.",
 "reading.club.hero.two_cities.2": "I read the last page twice. Aloud, quietly.",
 "line.town.bookclub.white_nights.1": "June, white nights, so White Nights. There are only four nights in it.",
 "line.town.bookclub.white_nights.2": "A dreamer who knows every house by sight. I greet mine too.",
 "line.town.bookclub.white_nights.3": "He's lonely but writes about it so funnily. That's me in the dorm.",
 "line.town.bookclub.white_nights.4": "Petersburg in summer when it never gets dark. Like our June by the sea.",
 "line.town.bookclub.white_nights.5": "Dostoevsky still young and tender. Few people know him like this.",
 "reading.club.hero.white_nights.1": "I read it on the promenade in June, and it was light till the end.",
 "reading.club.hero.white_nights.2": "I'm sorry for the Dreamer. And he's still happier than many.",
 "line.town.bookclub.twenty_thousand.1": "July, the sea, Jules Verne. Twenty Thousand Leagues, and everyone to the water.",
 "line.town.bookclub.twenty_thousand.2": "First everyone hunts a monster. The scholars argue like our staffroom.",
 "line.town.bookclub.twenty_thousand.3": "A professor and an assistant who classifies everything. That's me on fieldwork.",
 "line.town.bookclub.twenty_thousand.4": "Electricity in 1870 like magic. Nemo is the first hacker engineer.",
 "line.town.bookclub.twenty_thousand.5": "Verne takes a table of fish and makes an adventure of it. I'm learning.",
 "reading.club.hero.twenty_thousand.1": "Now I look at the sea and work out how far twenty thousand leagues is.",
 "reading.club.hero.twenty_thousand.2": "Conseil classifying things even in danger is my hero.",
 "line.town.bookclub.invisible_man.1": "August: The Invisible Man. It starts in snow, at a small inn.",
 "line.town.bookclub.invisible_man.2": "The landlady is a kindred soul. A guest in bandages, and she fusses with tea.",
 "line.town.bookclub.invisible_man.3": "The whole village gossips about one man. Sound familiar?",
 "line.town.bookclub.invisible_man.4": "Wells's optics are almost plausible. Almost. I did the maths.",
 "line.town.bookclub.invisible_man.5": "A comedy for the first chapters, then a chill down your spine. He knows how.",
 "reading.club.hero.invisible_man.1": "I kept looking round in empty streets all evening. Thanks, Wells.",
 "reading.club.hero.invisible_man.2": "I felt sorry for him at the end, though it was his own fault.",
 "line.town.bookclub.rubaiyat.1": "September: Khayyam. One quatrain each. Who chose which?",
 "line.town.bookclub.rubaiyat.2": "The clay jug that was once a man. I know that one by heart.",
 "line.town.bookclub.rubaiyat.3": "Wine, stars and \"don't be sad\". Khayyam is the best big brother.",
 "line.town.bookclub.rubaiyat.4": "He was a mathematician, he worked out a calendar. You hear it in the rhythm.",
 "line.town.bookclub.rubaiyat.5": "Four lines and a whole life. I wish I could do that in a paragraph.",
 "reading.club.hero.rubaiyat.1": "I copied one quatrain into my diary. About roses and dust.",
 "reading.club.hero.rubaiyat.2": "I read it on a bench, with those very stars overhead.",
 "line.town.bookclub.little_princess.1": "October: A Little Princess. Welcome, newcomers!",
 "line.town.bookclub.little_princess.2": "A girl at boarding school, papa far away. I saw such girls every September for forty years.",
 "line.town.bookclub.little_princess.3": "Sara makes up stories so she won't cry. Strong move.",
 "line.town.bookclub.little_princess.4": "Emily the doll who \"comes alive\" when no one looks. I like it.",
 "line.town.bookclub.little_princess.5": "Burnett writes a children's book in earnest. That's rare.",
 "reading.club.hero.little_princess.1": "I liked Sara because she never stops being polite.",
 "reading.club.hero.little_princess.2": "The attic with Melchisedec the rat — I'd live there.",
 "line.town.bookclub.dead_souls.1": "November: Gogol, Dead Souls. A britzka drives into town...",
 "line.town.bookclub.dead_souls.2": "Two peasants argue whether the wheel will make it to Moscow. Best opening in the world.",
 "line.town.bookclub.dead_souls.3": "Everyone likes Chichikov and nobody knows what he wants. Yet.",
 "line.town.bookclub.dead_souls.4": "He buys what doesn't exist. Almost like a startup.",
 "line.town.bookclub.dead_souls.5": "Gogol spends three pages on a tavern and I'm hungry. Magic.",
 "reading.club.hero.dead_souls.1": "I laughed out loud on the train and people turned round.",
 "reading.club.hero.dead_souls.2": "Plyushkin is frightening and sad at once. How can anyone write that?",
 "line.town.bookclub.christmas_carol.1": "December: A Christmas Carol. We read it before Christmas, no later!",
 "line.town.bookclub.christmas_carol.2": "\"Marley was dead, to begin with.\" That's how we taught a first line.",
 "line.town.bookclub.christmas_carol.3": "Scrooge won't let his clerk have more coal. I froze at once.",
 "line.town.bookclub.christmas_carol.4": "The door knocker turns into a face. A great glitch.",
 "line.town.bookclub.christmas_carol.5": "Short, one evening's worth. Dickens knew how long a winter evening is.",
 "reading.club.hero.christmas_carol.1": "I finished it in one evening, just as you said.",
 "reading.club.hero.christmas_carol.2": "After the book you want to bring someone coal. Or a pie.",
